  "scope": [
    "Turn the locally rehearsed WI-0118 protocol into a deterministic four-repository fixture and fail-closed experiment runner, then execute the frozen matched comparison only after exact Provider and account approval.",
    "Compare Temple with a competent minimal responsible workflow under identical repositories, task input, tests, tools, and model routes; measure organizational outcomes rather than pass counts.",
    "Stop at the bounded experiment report; do not change routing policy, release Temple, deploy services, or generalize from one scenario."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Four real local Git repositories are created from deterministic sources, pin exact revisions, and reproduce the seeded compatibility failure before candidate work.",
    "Both arms remain matched except for the declared organizational intervention, use zero retry and zero fallback, and fail closed on protocol, model, usage, command, or revision drift.",
    "The runner and analyzer retain objective correctness, cold recovery, boundary conflicts, contract convergence, rework, human intervention, operational and gross Tokens, latency, and artifact footprint.",
    "No Provider generation occurs until a final preflight publishes the exact protocol digest, requested models and efforts, maximum Tokens, maximum elapsed time, and receives matching human approval.",
    "The final report is descriptive, preserves stopped and negative outcomes, and makes no superiority, savings, pricing, or routing-authority claim beyond the observed run."
  ],
